= Poseidon

Poseidon is one of the twelve Olympian deities in Greek mythology, known as the god of the sea, earthquakes, storms, and horses. He is often depicted wielding a trident and is considered one of the most powerful gods in the Greek pantheon, second only to his brother Zeus.
